course: dictionary
lesson: 2954
title: Words in context: driveway
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A driveway is a short private road or paved area that leads from the street to a house or garage. Cars park on it. You can often work out the meaning from the words around it. Read this: «A driver reversing out of a driveway or a parking space may not see a child behind the car.» Cars are reversing out, so the driveway must be the place where the car starts from, next to the house.
explain: Look for clues about where things are. «Chalk drawings belong on your own driveway or a quiet path, never on the road where cars come.» Here the driveway is on your own property, near home, and the road is where the cars come. The clues tell you the driveway is not the main road.
explain: Some clues are about safety. «Drivers often do not see children, so try to catch the driver's eye.» A driveway is a place where cars are moving in and out, so you must be careful there. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A driveway leads from the street to a house or garage.
fact: Cars park on a driveway, and drivers often back out of it.
fact: Drivers reversing out of a driveway may not see a child behind the car, so never play behind or around a parked car.
fact: «Driveway» can also be used for a maths area: a driveway 12 m long and 3 m wide has an area of 36 m².
fact: In February 2021 a meteorite fell on a driveway in Winchcombe, Gloucestershire, and was picked up within hours.
exercise: «A driver reversing out of a driveway or a parking space may not see a child behind the car.» What is a driveway? | A park with swings and a slide | *A short private road or paved area from the street to a house | A big road with many lanes of fast traffic | A river that runs past the school
exercise: «A driver reversing out of a driveway or a parking space may not see a child behind the car.» What does reversing mean? | Stopping for a rest | Moving quickly forwards | *Moving backwards | Parking in the street
exercise: A driveway is 12 m long and 3 m wide. What is its area? | 24 m² | *36 m² | 9 m² | 15 m²
test: «In February 2021 a meteorite fell on a driveway in Winchcombe, Gloucestershire.» Where did the meteorite land? | *On a driveway | In the sea | On the roof of a school | In a field of wheat
test: You are walking on the pavement near a house. What should you do when you pass a driveway? | Play a game behind a parked car | Close your eyes | Run across it quickly | *Watch for cars coming out and wait until the driver has seen you
exam: Which of these is a driveway? | A wide road with lots of traffic | *A paved area beside a house where cars are parked | A path through a park | A short private road from the street to a house, where cars park
